WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.340
Hello everybody my name is Markiplier and welcome back to OneShot.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:09.000
Now, we left Niko in the darkness and Niko was saying something new that I'm not entirely sure I like,

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.940
"Oh Markiplier let me know when you're back..."

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.000
I'm back..
"I don't know why this keeps happening..."

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:21.000
Aaaah I'm sorry! I can't play it all in one sitting that's so sad...

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.740
"Oh I hope the squares don't spread too fast..."

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:30.640
Be the way, I showed him the book and I rescued his sister, but these people have been living alone for a while,

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.220
and their back room is full of dust and cobwebs...

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:38.460
So I just gotta keeping going forward and hopefully I won't need to leave Niko too much longer now...

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.620
Find out what's in the rest of these...

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.280
caverns they got going on here... woah...

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:45.420
huh...

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.340
"Hey!"

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.560
"I saw you go into the courtyard, so I thought I would tag along!"

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.020
"Same!"

00:00:52.020 --> 00:01:00.420
Alright... Okay then, just cause I'm in your backyard doesn't mean that I plan to do anything dastardly... like steal your clothes or nothin like that,

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.520
Just cause I'm not from this world.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:03.780
Oh wow...

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.820
So is this a never ending series of caaaaaverns?

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.780
Oh HI there mysterious children that follow me

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.260
"Looks like it used to lead somewhere."

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.600
"Yeah the sacred grounds! It's been a while since we went there."

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.680
"We don't have any way of getting there now remember?" "There isn't a boat and none of us can swim."

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.200
"There isn't a boat and none of us can swim."

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.120
"What's the sacred grounds?"

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.120
"It's where our people are buried."

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.560
"Sometimes we go there to visit mom.... Well, her grave anyway..."

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.520
"Oh..."

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.540
"Wait how do you get there? I thought you said there isn't a boat?"

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:35.960
"Oh, our friend helps us!

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.720
"He has some sort of machine that allows him to fly."

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.320
"Sometimes he takes us along!"

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:41.880
Aren't you birds?

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.320
Don't you have wings and feathers?

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:47.860
"Like I was about to say, we haven't seen him around for a while."

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.280
"I wonder when he'll come back... I wish we could go see mom again..."

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:52.660
Oh...

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.260
"Come on, Alula, let's get back to the courtyard."

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:01.800
My god I didn't shout the word Alula. It's a breakthrough! Cm'on sis... "Okay."

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:03.360
Man.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.340
That's so sad though...

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:11.840
Maybe death is like a common concept in this world because the whole world's dying.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:12.980
"It's a ball."

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.520
"That's mine!" Don't touch it... "It doesn't bounce as much as it used to though."

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.660
*bell ringing*
BING BONG!!

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:20.460
Hi, fishy.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:21.860
"Fish!" FISH!

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:23.120
Can I have some???

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.120
I'm quite ravenous as a...

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.760
fellow fish eater...

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.260
Being a cat and all

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:29.840
Man...

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.100
"You leaving now? Good luck Niko, we believe in you."

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:38.280
"Are you leaving? It was nice to meet you, really, thanks for everything."

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.700
Well god man, that's so sad...

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:45.780
Well who's the guy who helped you...fly?

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.600
Oh that's so sad...

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.880
Oh well I guess I gotta press forward. Maybe I can take the sun back now?

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:57.640
Cause I've already made my way down here so I guess that I don't really need to do...

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:02.200
...anything else. Gotta go find... *sigh*

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:07.980
Gotta take that to the tower and fix this world, but then again like it's just so sad to think about that...

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.880
Maybe this world can't be fixed? So why am I here?

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.140
Oh...

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.160
"She's gone"

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:18.200
Oh...

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.400
There's something on the ground? It looks like a kernel of corn?

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.700
"She must have left it behind"

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.240
The Seed?

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.160
"The light's gone out!"

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:30.060
Eah!

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.160
"Markiplier!"

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.580
"Do you know what happened?"

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:33.760
No!

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:34.940
"You...really?"

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:41.580
I-I know I-I I'm supposedly all knowing but in this one instance, I don't have an ideaaa...

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.380
"What am I gonna do?"

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.740
Oh! There it goes. You just had to touch it.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:49.000
"It lit up again?"

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:50.080
"...phew."

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.720
Yeah it only lights when you touch it Niko-- oh my god...

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:59.960
But what if that means that Niko has to stay at the tower, and the reason the light went out last time was because...

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:02.620
The last person died...

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:09.840
I mean that's a morbid thought and I have no evidence to that idea, but...

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.840
Following logic...

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:16.280
They wouldn't actually do that, would they?

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:18.340
That'd be heartbreaking...

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:22.140
But then again, there's a lot of themes of death in this game...

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:24.320
They wouldn't do that...?

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:26.140
They wouldn't-

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.380
They wouldn't do that, would they?

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:34.380
Oh! I know what I need to do! The feather and the bottle of dye, I can use it as a pen.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:39.260
And then a seed, left behind by Maize, who-- Maize is

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:42.160
corn, that means corn I think in Spanish

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:45.560
And also in other countries it's called maize as well, but

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:50.120
So now I can take this pen and bottle of ink and then I can use it, or I can use it as a pen,

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:54.320
and I can take it over to the robot, and hopefully he's not gonna smack me with his giant scroooll...

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.020
...and then I'll be able to progress further.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:04.520
At least they gave me a lucky glowing feather, and this sacred feather that they've given me, trusted with me...

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.080
One that they've held onto

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:09.220
from their dead father, and I'm gonna use it as a pen.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:13.000
The first thing that I did, literary the first thing I did was dip it in ink

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.340
So good job for me, I'm an asshole...

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:20.180
"Markiplier, I'm too tired to go on right now...please let me nap for a bit somewhere."

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:22.940
I-

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.320
I don't know where to...let you nap

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:30.460
there was a bed back in the kids' place, do you wanna...

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:31.380
nap there?

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.100
They had three, I mean-

00:05:34.340 --> 00:05:36.900
I don't know whose bed was the spare?

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.540
I guess we'll go there, then.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:41.200
"It's a bed."

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:43.320
Dammit.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:45.520
Not these beds, alright then...

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:47.840
Gotta find...somewhere to sleep.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:52.320
Do I remember seeing and of those special light bulb beds anywhere, cause I do not.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:54.620
Unfortunately...

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:57.120
Ooh, hello

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.060
OH!

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:00.660
Well that's convenient, it was led to by the clovers...

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.060
I don't remember this even being here before.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:04.160
"I'm a little tired from walking."

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.160
"Is it alright if I take a nap?"

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:07.320
Yes?

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.320
Goodbye! I guess?

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.400
Oh.

00:06:16.280 --> 00:06:16.780
Huh...

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:18.300
Run...

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:20.400
Oh.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:25.120
That's so sad.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:26.800
"Markiplier, I had another dream!"

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.200
"Did you see this one too?"

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:29.360
Yeah!

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:31.360
"I was in a big field, like the one in my last dream..."

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:35.360
"And... I saw my village!... but then I woke up."

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:38.280
"*sigh*, I don't think this world has anything like that..."

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:39.780
"I mean, big wheat fields!"

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.840
"The only big plants I've seen here are a bunch of weird trees."

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:45.240
"And those balls of moss floating in the water."

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:47.020
"Wait, is moss even a plant...?"

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.900
"Say, have you seen a wheat field before, Markiplier?"

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:52.000
YES I HAVE!

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:54.180
"Oh! They're really pretty, aren't they?"

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:57.160
"The one around my village goes around for miles!"

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.980
"The plants are really tall, sometimes I can't even see through them!"

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.480
"When it's windy out, the wind can make waves in it."

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:05.620
"It's like an ocean..."

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:06.660
"Of food..."

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:08.940
"Oh, wait, but there's food in regular oceans too..."

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:10.940
"Like fish, or crabs!"

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:13.220
"I've never actually been to a real ocean until now, actually..."

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.360
I've been to the ocean, oh yes.

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.040
"That's really cool!"

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.040
"I've only seen the ocean on TV before."

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.080
"I never thought I'd get to ride a boat through one!"

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.860
"The water back home doesn't have the glowy stuff like how it is here, either!"

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:28.880
"Ah... but I guess it's because the world is already so dark..."

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:31.160
"...Y'know I used to be scared of the dark, Markiplier!"

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:34.920
"It's a little hard to imagine that now, after spending so much time here..."

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:38.140
"But not long ago, I couldn't even go to sleep without a lamp..."

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:40.600
Aww...

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.140
It's good you got over that!

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:44.980
"I guess! Otherwise I wouldn't last long here..."

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.920
"Then again, I've been carrying around the sun, so it's not too bad!"

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:50.260
"And also, I don't feel scared at all with you guiding me!"

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.260
MAYBE YOU SHOULD...

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:53.680
I'm not the best guide...

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:54.560
...so thanks for that.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:56.560
"Anyway, maybe we should head out now, Markiplier..."

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:58.560
Alright, ok, whatever you say.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.480
Now we gotta get over to this guy.

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.560
Gotta sign up a thing!

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.560
Oop, that's wrong- there we go!

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:05.520
HELLO!

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:07.300
I found a pen! Sort of...

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:09.960
"Good. Please write your name here."

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:13.820
*Imitates writing*

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:14.760
Got it.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:16.760
"Good luck."

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:18.960
THANK YOOOU!

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:19.800
I think?

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.800
I don't know where I'm going now, but

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:23.120
THANK YOOOU!

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:26.360
Woooah, why am I walking on the ramparts?

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:27.540
Euh.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:28.540
WHAAA?

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:30.920
"What in the world..?"

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:32.300
Euh.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.200
I thought it was going to chase me for a second there...

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:38.200
I guess I can't go back, though.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:41.480
Okay...

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:43.480
Alright then I guess that's just happening now.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:44.780
Ugh.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:47.060
Ayy. No no no no-

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.900
Ah nono. NONOnonononono.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:50.040
That's baaad.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:51.620
No no no, don't do that.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.420
That's no good. That's no bueno.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:55.700
Oh.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:56.700
Whoa.

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.900
I've made it to the city already?

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:06.400
That's so weird because that whole other place was just me talking to these people.

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:09.280
Woah.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:14.280
Oh that's- That's thumpy. That's got a good thump to it.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.400
Ah, that's real parallaxy too.

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:18.840
Ah- "Ah, the sun."

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:22.100
"Hello Messiah. Welcome to the Refuge."

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.240
"Do you understand what you must do here?"

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.900
"I'm supposed to go inside the tower, right?

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:29.240
"I already see the tower, so I guess we must be close."

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:30.320
"Where's the entrance?"

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:31.520
"On the surface!"

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:32.760
"The surface?"

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.100
"Look down, small one!"

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.480
"Ooooh, we're pretty high up."

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:39.480
"I guess I gotta go down a lot of stairs!"

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:40.600
"Or find an elevator."

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:41.680
"Correct."

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.840
"However, the tower is a... sacred place."

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:48.400
"Finding the entrance may be easy, but that alone will not be enough!"

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.120
"Whaddyou mean?"

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:53.860
"Once you reach the Surface, I recommend visiting the library for leads."

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:55.540
"Alright, thank you!"

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:58.500
"Off you go, then! I wish you luck!"

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:00.200
Mmm, okay

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:03.320
"I'm afraid this area is off-limits for you!"

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:07.880
Gonna, smash your head in with my giant robot fists if you go any farther!

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:11.740
"Only the bearer of the sacred kernel is permitted access to the garden."

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:13.420
I've got a...

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:15.780
I've got a seed, is it sacred?

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:17.340
What about the seed?

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:20.040
"Oh, like a kernel of... CORN?"

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:23.760
"I have this! It was left behind by a plant lady in the Glen."

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:26.460
"That is indeed the kernel!"

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:28.960
"Then it is your duty to regrow her!"

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:30.420
"Do you understand what you must do?"

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:31.500
No. Not at all.

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:32.640
No, I don- I don't.

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:33.260
No.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:36.200
"Take the seed to the garden! Plant it in the pot in the center!"

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:39.280
"You may now pass through here to access the garden."

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:41.840
Alrighty then!

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:43.300
Thank youuuuu!

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:45.840
Where's this pot you were talking about?

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:47.560
Mmm.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:49.200
Ok.

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:50.360
Oh!

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:52.860
Why would she regrow here?

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:57.020
"There's no dirt in this pot."

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:57.760
Will the seed really grow-

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:00.040
Ohhhhh, I see it!

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.300
I got a tube of water but no dirt!

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.960
Ahh! Did anybody see a pile of dirt around here?

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:06.100
Dirt?

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.620
It's about yeigh high!

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:08.840
Looks like DIRT!

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:09.800
EHHHH?

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:11.460
Pile... it's in a pile!

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:12.820
Answers to the name

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:13.540
DIRT!

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:16.120
Pile O' Dirt, maybe?

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.640
You know, by its maiden name!

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:21.220
If anybody has seen it, just let me know, if anybody has seen a pile of dirt-

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:22.280
Why is there no floor here?

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.720
Alright then, I have no commentary about that!

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:25.980
Just looking for a PILE OF DIRT!

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:27.900
Anybody got some dirt? Anybody?

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:28.400
You?

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:29.080
He? She?

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:29.780
Got dirt?

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:30.380
We?

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:32.180
Anybody? Ok, alright.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:32.940
Woah!

00:11:34.100 --> 00:11:35.180
"COME ONNNNNNNN!"

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:36.220
*Various crashing noises*

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:38.360
"COM'ONNNNNNNN''

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:39.700
"WORK ALREADY!"

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:41.600
"Huh? What was that?"

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.280
I don't know. Someone angry!

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:44.020
'Bout something!

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:45.120
Might be Markiplier.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.320
Have you ever thought of that?

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:47.380
Oh, hello!

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:49.280
"Come onnnn!"

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:50.720
"Come OooOOoOnNNNnnNn!"

